  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Robbie Ray held them to one run through six innings, and the offense finally broke through in the seventh when it mattered.",
    "what_this_means": "Ray gave them air to work with. A clean start against a Pirates lineup that stayed quiet until the late innings forced some drama. Ten strikeouts and a single earned run is the kind of line that wins games. The offense didn't explode, but it didn't need to. Devers hit one for real, Ramos added a hit with runners in motion, and when the seventh inning came, they pushed three across. That was the game decided. It wasn't comfortable. It was just enough, and that's the formula that has kept them treading water all season. A good starter and enough bats late. Nothing more, nothing less. They've beaten this pattern before. Not yet, though.",
